# Store Stock Management — Frontend Docs

Base namespace (web views)
- Categories: /admin/categories
- Items: /admin/items

Note: These are Laravel resource routes returning HTML. For SPA/JSON, send `Accept: application/json` (to receive JSON validation errors/responses) or expose dedicated API endpoints.

## Product Categories

Routes
- GET /admin/categories — List (paginated)
- GET /admin/categories/create — Create form
- POST /admin/categories — Create
- GET /admin/categories/{id} — Details
- GET /admin/categories/{id}/edit — Edit form
- PUT /admin/categories/{id} — Update
- DELETE /admin/categories/{id} — Delete

Fields (form/JSON keys)
- name string (required, unique)
- description string (optional)

Validation
- name: required, unique

## Stock Items

Routes
- GET /admin/items — List (paginated, includes category name)
- GET /admin/items/create — Create form (category dropdown prefilled)
- POST /admin/items — Create
- GET /admin/items/{id} — Details
- GET /admin/items/{id}/edit — Edit form
- PUT /admin/items/{id} — Update
- DELETE /admin/items/{id} — Delete

Fields (form/JSON keys)
- name string (required)
- product_category_id integer (required; must exist)
- primary_unit string (required)
- secondary_unit string (required)
- qty_per_primary_unit integer (>= 1)
- qty_per_secondary_unit integer (>= 1)
- last_purchase_price number (>= 0)
- selling_price number (>= 0)
- image_url string (optional)

Validation
- name: required
- product_category_id: required, exists
- primary_unit, secondary_unit: required
- qty_per_*: integer, min 1
- last_purchase_price, selling_price: numeric, min 0

## HTML Form Field Names
- Category: name, description
- Item: name, product_category_id, primary_unit, secondary_unit, qty_per_primary_unit, qty_per_secondary_unit, last_purchase_price, selling_price, image_url

## Examples (SPA / fetch)

Create Category
```javascript
await fetch('/admin/categories', {
  method: 'POST',
  headers: {
    'Content-Type': 'application/json',
    'Accept': 'application/json',
    'X-CSRF-TOKEN': document.querySelector('meta[name="csrf-token"]').content
  },
  body: JSON.stringify({ name: 'Cement', description: 'All cement types' })
});
```

Create Stock Item
```javascript
await fetch('/admin/items', {
  method: 'POST',
  headers: {
    'Content-Type': 'application/json',
    'Accept': 'application/json',
    'X-CSRF-TOKEN': document.querySelector('meta[name="csrf-token"]').content
  },
  body: JSON.stringify({
    name: 'Portland Cement',
    product_category_id: 1,
    primary_unit: 'bag',
    secondary_unit: 'kg',
    qty_per_primary_unit: 50,
    qty_per_secondary_unit: 1,
    last_purchase_price: 1200.00,
    selling_price: 1400.00,
    image_url: 'https://cdn.example.com/img/cement.jpg'
  })
});
```

## Category Dropdown Data
- Server-rendered forms already receive `$categories = ProductCategory::orderBy('name')->pluck('name','id')`.
- SPA option (add API if needed): expose `GET /api/product-categories` returning `[ { id, name } ]` for dropdowns.

## JSON Responses (optional SPA mode)
- Send `Accept: application/json` to receive JSON on success and 422 validation errors.
- Standard Laravel validation error shape:
```json
{
  "message": "The given data was invalid.",
  "errors": { "name": ["The name field is required."] }
}
```

## Success Redirects vs JSON
- Current controllers redirect after create/update/delete for server-rendered pages.
- For SPA, either:
  - Handle 302 by following redirect, or
  - Switch to API endpoints that return JSON 200/201 without redirects.

## Stock Refunds (API)
- POS sale refunds: `POST /api/customers/{customer}/sales/{sale}/refunds`
  - Body: `{ items: [{ sale_item_id, quantity }], note?, refund_date? }`
  - Replenishes stock, writes a `customer_transactions` refund entry, debits revenue + LOSS-001, and pays the customer back from `CASH-001` (no advance credit).
- Invoice refunds: `POST /api/invoices/{invoice}/refunds`
  - Body: `{ items: [{ invoice_item_id, quantity, unit_type? }], note?, refund_date? }`
  - Uses the same unit type that was sold, restocks inventory, updates invoice totals, and books the payout against the same deposit account that collected the invoice (fallback: `CASH-001`).
- Both endpoints automatically reduce the customer's due balance; any remainder is paid out immediately rather than being stored as customer advance.